Explain the difference between a forward proxy and a reverse proxy using real-life analogies?


💌 𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐝 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐱𝐲 𝐀𝐧𝐚𝐥𝐨𝐠𝐲

You (𝐂𝐥𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐭) love a girl (𝐖𝐞𝐛𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐞), but you're too shy or restricted to contact her directly (𝐞.𝐠., 𝐛𝐥𝐨𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐝 𝐛𝐲 𝐚 𝐟𝐢𝐫𝐞𝐰𝐚𝐥𝐥 𝐨𝐫 𝐧𝐞𝐞𝐝 𝐚𝐧𝐨𝐧𝐲𝐦𝐢𝐭𝐲).

 So, you write a love letter and give it to a kid (𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐝 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐱𝐲).
 The kid delivers it to the girl, she reads it and replies — again via the kid.

 You never talk to her directly, but she gets your message.

🧠 Key idea:

 The proxy works on behalf of the client, hiding the client from the destination (𝐥𝐢𝐤𝐞 𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐩𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐱𝐢𝐞𝐬 𝐨𝐫 𝐕𝐏𝐍𝐬).


🧑💼 𝐑𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐞 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐱𝐲 𝐀𝐧𝐚𝐥𝐨𝐠𝐲

You (𝐂𝐥𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐭) want to meet the CEO (𝐁𝐚𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐧𝐝 𝐒𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐫) of a company.
 But you’re stopped by the PA (𝐑𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐞 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐱𝐲).

 The PA listens to your request, decides which internal department (𝐛𝐚𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐧𝐝 𝐬𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐫) to send it to.
 The PA gets the reply from the CEO (𝐨𝐫 𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐭𝐞𝐚𝐦) and hands it back to you.


🧠 Key idea:

 The reverse proxy works on behalf of the server, hiding the backend and acting as the gatekeeper.


